    "lawCode": "Amd §§512, 608 & 1209, R & SS L; amd §13-638.4, NYC Ad Cd",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8490\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law and the adminis-\ntrative code of the city of New York, in relation to the calculation of\nthe final average salary for purposes of the calculation of a pension\nbenefit\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation will provide members of the public retirement systems\nin tiers five and six with similar benefits already received by tier 4\nas it relates to the calculation of their final average salary, provid-\ning pension equity to these members.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill amends subdivision section 512 of the retirement\nand Social Security law to adjust the final average salary calculation\nfor members the New York State and Local Retirement System.\n\nSection 2 of the legislation amends section 608 of the retirement and\nsocial security law, to adjust the final average salary calculation for\nmembers of the New York State Teachers' Retirement System and the New\nYork City Teachers' Retirement System.\n\nSection 3 of the legislation amends section 13-638.4 of the administra-\ntive code of the city of New York to adjust the final average salary\ncalculation for members of the New York City Employees Retirement\nSystem.\n\nSection 4 of the legislation amends section 1209 of the retirement and\nsocial security law to adjust the final average salary of the New York\nState and Local Police and Fire Retirement System.\n\nSection 5 the legislation notwithstands section 25 the retirement and\nsocial security law. Section 6 of the legislation is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTier 6 of the public pension system provide significantly reduced bene-\nfits when compared to previous tiers.  Public employees hired on or\nafter April 1, 2012, must work many years longer and pay larger percent-\nages of their salaries into the system, and yet they will still earn\nsignificantly less in retirement than their counterparts in tier 4.\n\nTwo years ago, the legislature enacted the first change to tier 6 since\nits creation - the reduction of the vesting requirements from 10 to five\nyears of service. This change guaranteed pension benefits to tens of\nthousands of public employees. While this was a good first step, there\nare more corrective actions that must be put in place to fix tier 6,\nsuch as amendments contained in this legislation.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee attached fiscal note.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately.\n",
